{"sequence":14,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:39:08.719321916Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-2857eb23","body":"FIX: SUB_ADULT_FEEDING_WEIGHT is defined as 0.65 in crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs:148 but 0.67 in crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:15. The shrimp.rs constant is the one used by the actual simulation (feeding, condition, mortality). The biology.rs constant is used by public API methods feeding_units(), add_reserve_by_feeding_units(). These must be unified to a single source-of-truth constant to prevent silent divergence when the public API is called.","dedup_key":"47b3d6ded9f74249a0ab227b1392f7ad6487389070f423b8cd97759a7129201e","run_id":"run-20260328125535","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":15,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:39:08.728284440Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-b5357512","body":"FIX: Test trim_plants_is_closed_system_via_helpers (crates/tank_core/tests/budget_helpers.rs:242-266) asserts N/C conservation for TrimPlantsAndRemove, but the whole purpose of that action variant is to EXPORT biomass from the system. The test should either: (a) use TrimPlantsAndLeaveCuttings instead (which is the conserving variant), or (b) assert that total N/C decreases by exactly the exported amount. Additionally, line 259 searches for budget label 'action:trim_plants' which likely doesn't match the actual label 'action:trim_plants_and_remove'. This test currently FAILS.","dedup_key":"2cab16e841e1c02c742a6b737a8ecec308b96d0d92e4b9869193775928a26d84","run_id":"run-20260328125535","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":16,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:39:08.733123715Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-264c0ac6","body":"Update the stale trim-budget helper test in `crates/tank_core/tests/budget_helpers.rs:242-264`. It still treats `PlayerAction::TrimPlantsAndRemove` as a closed-system redistribution and looks up the old budget label `action:trim_plants`, but the engine now implements export semantics for that action in `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:600-639` and records it as `action:trim_plants_and_remove` (`crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:791-792`). This currently breaks `cargo test` with `trim_plants_is_closed_system_via_helpers`. Either switch the test to `TrimPlantsAndLeaveCuttings` and the new label, or keep `TrimPlantsAndRemove` and assert net N/C export instead of conservation.","dedup_key":"db5e58ae6e26094fd1f66cd646ed5d0496aac57a546b30fb6c3a982537227047","run_id":"run-20260328125535","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":17,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:39:08.742082822Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-f4085f8d","body":"Fix `crates/tank_core/tests/plant_algae_integration.rs:195-217`, which still asserts that `PlayerAction::TrimPlantsAndRemove` increases `fine_detritus_g_total`. That contradicts the implementation in `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:600-639`, where only `TrimPlantsAndLeaveCuttings` routes biomass to detritus and `TrimPlantsAndRemove` exports it. The test fails as written; it should either use `TrimPlantsAndLeaveCuttings` for a detritus-routing scenario or change its assertions to verify exported biomass/no detritus increase for the remove variant.","dedup_key":"e3b916eae21a7a0a4844804ec05e5ce55dd561309af6531eeae7e2b7b78f8922","run_id":"run-20260328125535","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
